# ⭐ NARROW-TABLE EQUIVALENT of the reverted step-transfer construct
#
# WHAT IT IS
#   Reproduces, from the 3-wide LUT, exactly the actions the 6-wide LUT emitted in slots
#   3..5 — so it inherits that construct's measured income WITHOUT its .rodata growth,
#   which was the measured cause of the revert.
#
# WHY IT WORKS (the mechanism, which is the whole point)
#   `_build_slut` pre-folds early arrival: for a target at distance d it sets
#   fact[t] = fact[t-1] ^ 1 for every t >= d. So once a unit reaches its target the later
#   slots are a STATIONARY OSCILLATION — off, back, off — re-entering the same cell. Since
#   pickup is proportional (ceil(0.65v) taken, floor(0.35v) left), that oscillation re-mills
#   the 35% residue on the cell just harvested. THE VALUE IS RESIDUE, NOT REACH.
#   The 6-wide table therefore paid 448 bytes of .rodata to store what is one XOR.
#
# THE RULE, and its two non-obvious guards
#   after 3 steps, recompute the offset to the same target:
#     offset == 0 (arrived) AND pa[2] != STAY  ->  emit  pa2^1, pa2, pa2^1
#     offset == 0 AND pa[2] == STAY            ->  emit  STAY,STAY,STAY
#     offset != 0 (not arrived)                ->  re-enter the SAME 3-wide table
#   GUARD 1: at d == 0 the 6-wide table is ALSO all-STAY, because its fold is gated on
#            d > 0. So "alternate on arrival" must not fire there.
#   GUARD 2: STAY is action 4 and 4 ^ 1 == 5, an ILLEGAL action code. The pa[2] != STAY
#            test is a safety requirement, not a nicety.
#   No passability check on the tail, matching the 6-wide construct, which also emitted
#   slots 3..5 unchecked (the engine skips illegal moves).
#
# EQUIVALENCE — proven two ways
#   1. DOMAIN ARGUMENT (required by our own rule, since pair_diff is evidence not proof):
#      exhaustive over all 49 LUT cells, the rule reproduces the 6-wide slots 3..5 with
#      0 mismatches.
#   2. pair_diff against the reverted construct: 0/500 on three real platform logs
#      (game_140519 / 140521 / 140523).
#
# VERIFIED FIGURES (contest machine, GCC 14.3.1, -O3 -march=native, zero warnings)
#   .rodata 1360  <- BYTE-IDENTICAL to fd47ea6; the revert cause is eliminated
#   .text   5410  (+143 hot total, versus +464 for the reverted construct)
#   same-stream instructions 799.802  (baseline 802.804, so -3.00, BELOW baseline)
#   pad 80  ->  entry 0x1a10, mod64 == 0x10      FP16 0
#   .text sha256 da9d960053d8a1fa2330fa85eeb6b503...
#   income: +111.3 +/- 16.0 INHERITED by bit-identical behaviour, gate 32.1, OOS +79.8,
#           joint move (opponent -5.2). NOT independently re-measured.
#
# ⛔ NOT MEASURED, AND THIS IS THE ONLY REMAINING GATE
#   PLATFORM latency. Footprint scaling suggests about +10 ns of P50 (the reverted
#   construct measured +33 ns at +464 bytes), but that is a PROXY, and tonight proved
#   proxies here can err by sign (-42 instructions measured +33 ns) and by 70x. Only an
#   interleaved same-window platform control (base and candidate submitted alternately,
#   same opponents and maps, three maps, strictly serial) can decide.
#   DO NOT LAND OR PUBLISH THIS WITHOUT THAT CONTROL.
#
